			<div class="content" id="post-content-3622029">
									

<p>Promising: moments of flair and strong exploration of a relatively strong idea.</p>
<p>It is far too long for me, however. Much of what you have here feels like it's repeating the same ideas over and over. I didn't get much sense of progression from the interviews, for instance. You could easily have cut one of the three interview logs, and pared down the nightmare imagery to just the most evocative examples. The integration of submarine control with -1's proprioception was neat and plausibly described, but again, you could have boiled down all of that recording log to the most essential and effective elements.</p>
<p>For me, organisations, especially Soviets, putting consciousnesses inside military equipment is beginning to feel played out on here. (<a href="/scp-1984">SCP-1984</a> is the most famous example.)</p>
<p>Dialogue varied in quality. I get the sense that you were very much writing from your own voice; I didn't hear a consistent, unique tone ringing out from -2, and amongst other things, his fluency seemed ill-fitting for a recent Soviet defector. You could have had fun sprinkling in a few Russianisms in vocabulary and grammar. Again, reducing the dialogue down to the best bits would have improved the varying quality. Some genuinely good bits here and there, though.</p>
<p>&quot;Cyrillic written sentences&quot; written on the walls by -1, and then very English language–specific typos – not sure how this works. Not written in Russian, right? Written in English but with Cyrillic letters? If so, clarify.</p>
<p>Last note didn't do much for me. I think it's partly because it was a little too long, so it didn't wasn't as punchy as it could have been. Perhaps also because it feels a little unsatisfying to have some undescribed, unforeshadowed walk-in deliver the epilogue.</p>
<p>There's plenty I did like: imagery (particularly the momentary appearance of that bust of Lenin), scientific realism, formatting, much of the core idea (biological submarine was fun to read about), scientific tone in the prose. Lots of promise, but would have really benefited from a lot of hard-nosed, aggressive editing.</p>
<p>Also made some SPaG edits. Feel free to overrule the full stops if you'd prefer it without.</p>

							</div>

								
					
